          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+geometry"} complex geometry
            %em Oka-Grauert principle
            states that over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifolds"} complex manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            which are
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stein+manifolds"} Stein manifolds
            = succeed "-classification" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+cohomology"} non-abelian cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+vector+bundles"} holomorphic vector bundles
            coincides with that of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundles"} topological vector bundles
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext is Stein
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ;
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mi GL
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ̲
                    %mi hol
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ;
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mi GL
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ̲
                    %mi top
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S \;\text{is Stein}
                  \\;\;\;\;\;
                  \\Rightarrow
                  \\;\;\;\;\;
                  H^1
                  \\Big(
                  S;
                  \\,
                  \\underline{GL(n, \mathbb{C})}_{hol}
                  \\Big)
                  \\,\simeq\,
                  H^1
                  \\Big(
                  S;
                  \\,
                  \\underline{GL(n, \mathbb{C})}_{top}
                  \\Big)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This was originally proven for holomorphic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundles"} line bundles
            by
            %a{:href => "#Oka39"} Oka 1939
            (in which case it says that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+line+bundles"} holomorphic line bundles
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stein+manifolds"} Stein manifolds
            are fully classified by their
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            %a{:href => "#Grauert58"} Grauert 1958
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+vector+bundles"} holomorphic vector bundles
            and further to holomorphic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+group"} structure group
            any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+Lie+group"} complex Lie group
          %p
            As a principle, this
            %em Oka-Grauert principle
            is sometimes stated as follows (
            %a{:href => "#Forstneric12"}> Forstnerič 2012
            ):
          %blockquote
            %p
              Analytic problems on Stein spaces which can be cohomologically formulated have only topological
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstructions"} obstructions
          %p
            More generally, for suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifolds"} complex manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            now called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oka+manifolds"} Oka manifolds
            (
            %a{:href => "#Forstneric09a"}> Forstnerič 2009a
            ) – including (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Oka+manifold#ComplexProjectiveSpaceIsOkaManifold"} here
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmannians"} Grassmannians
            that serve as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+spaces"} classifying spaces
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundles"} complex vector bundles
            –, the inclusion into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact-open+topology"} space of continuous maps
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \to A
