            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              This is the case precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Maps
                      %mi hol
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Psh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SteinSp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps_{hol}(-,X) \in Psh_\infty(SteinSp)
              satisfies
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
              with respect to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covers"} covers
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Larusson01"}> Larusson 01, theorem 2.1
            )
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              The category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifolds"} complex manifolds
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+maps"} holomorphic maps
              can be embedded into a Quillen
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              such that:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a holomorphic map is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
                  in the ambient model category if and only if it is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
                  in the usual topological sense;
              %li
                %p
                  a holomorphic map is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
                  if and only if it is an Oka map. In particular, a complex manifold is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant
                  if and only if it is an
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oka+manifold"} Oka manifold
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant"} cofibrant
                  if and only if it is
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stein+manifold"} Stein
              %li
                %p
                  a Stein inclusion is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration"} cofibration
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Larusson03"} Larusson 03
            – apparently this follows an observation due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+F.+Jardine"} J. F. Jardine
            and uses his
            = succeed ")" do
